Required Updates:
	Re-submission of the RMP must occur at least every five (5) years;
	A Hazard Review will be performed every five (5) years, or prior to implementation of a new or changed process.
	A compliance review will be conducted every three (3) years to review the facilitys compliance with the program requirements.
	The EPA lists a new substance that is present at the facility in excess of the threshold quantity  submit within three (3) years of listing;
	Employees that work with covered processes must receive refresher training at least every three (3) years; and
	The Emergency Response Information must be reviewed and updated annually.

Triggers for Action:
	The facility begins using a new regulated substance above the established threshold quantity  submit no later than the date the substance is present above the threshold quantity;
	The facility increases inventory of an existing regulated substance above the threshold quantity  submit no later than the date the substance is present above the threshold quantity;
	A hazard review requires a process change  submit no later than six (6) months from the change;
	The facility revises the offsite consequence analysis (Hazard Assessment section of the RMP)  submit within six (6) months of the change;
	A change at the facility alters the program level  submit within six (6) months;
	An incident that resulted in, or may have resulted in a near miss, the release of a regulated substance requires that an incident investigation be initiated no later than 48 hours after the incident; 
	An accidental release occurs or an implementing agency requires a third-party audit due to conditions that could lead to an accidental release (near miss) or when a previous third-party failed to meet the competency or independence requirement
